Note = {Annual Meeting of the Southern-Political-Science-Association, SAVANNAH,
   GEORGIA, NOV 03-06, 1999},
Organization = {SO Polit Sci Assoc},
Abstract = {While much empirical research has been devoted to the study of ``killer
   amendments{''} in recent years, few studies hake explicitly examined the
   theoretical foundations of the phenomenon, The goal of this paper is to
   investigate why some killer amendment attempts are successful. when
   theory suggests that the,, should always fail, More specifically. we
   examine the practical political constraints on legislators' abilities to
   neutralize the imminent threat of killer amendment, through
   sophisticated voting. We also present two new cases, both occurring
   during the Reconstruction era, in A which killer amendments were used
   successfully. In the end. our findings support precious research on all
   successful killer amendments detailed in the congressional literature:
   race was the issue under consideration at the amendment stage.},
